{
  "dom_id": "step-q38384",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}-1?$",
  "worked_solution": "To obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}-1,$ we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/d078ff010c5bb8a05bfe08bd6585ebb334bda324c69f7c8498bde38dbd8cd234.png)\n\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/2832645bc8cac13094899294dcd0cb45b24fb0da8339d5bc9e1e2c055aaee2b8.png)",
